\par }\pard\plain \s64\fi-1191\li1191\widctlpar\tx1191 \f5\fs22\lang2057 SOURCE:\tab Co-chair objective testgroup, John Beerends KPN Research
\par 
\par TITLE:\tab Evaluation of new methods for objective testing of video quality: objective test plan revised
\par 
\par \pard \s64\qc\fi-1191\li1191\widctlpar\tx1191 {\b Abstract
\par }\pard\plain \sb136\widctlpar\tx794\tx1191\tx1588\tx1985 \f5\fs22\lang2057 
This contribution presents an objective test plan that has been drafted by members of the VQEG (Video Quality Experts Group) ad hoc committee for the objective test plan. This test plan was offered to the participating ITU Study Groups (ITU-T Study Groups
 9 and 12 and ITU-R Study Group 11) for further review and comment. It was further modified during the 
second VQEG meeting (Gaithersburg USA May 1998), taking into account their comments. The objective test plan will be used to evaluate video quality in the bit rate range of 768 kbit/s to 50 Mbit/s. In conjunction with the subjective test plan, it will be 
used to evaluate several proposed methods for objectively assessing video quality by measuring the correlation between subjective and objective assessments. It is expected that parts of this test plan will be included in new Draft Recommendations in the a
rea of video quality, probably as an Annex.
\par 
\par \pard \qc\sb136\widctlpar\tx794\tx1191\tx1588\tx1985 {\b\fs28 
\par \page 
\par VQEG OBJECTIVE VIDEO QUALITY MODEL TEST PLAN
\par }\pard \sb136\widctlpar\tx794\tx1191\tx1588\tx1985 {\fs24 
